# Rule: the type ramps by role (ADR-092)

Full rule: `.claude/rules/type-material.md`. The short form:

- `letter-spacing` is `var(--track-copy|display|label|eyebrow)` or `0`. Never a
  literal; never a legacy `--track-wide`-style name (they are aliases that die at
  stage 4).
- Nothing above `--weight-lit` (500). **PT Mono has no 500** — a mono 700 is
  DELETED, not set to 500; emphasis on mono is ink. Sans display takes 500.
- The `font:` shorthand carries a weight; the ratchet scans it too.
- No `text-transform: uppercase` on PP Neue Montreal. PT Mono chrome stays
  uppercase. Check the string is AUTHORED sentence case first.
- **The HUD frame is the datum and is never swept**: `hud.css`, `navigation*.css`,
  `rail-instruments.css`, and the `.hud*` / `.rail-manifest*` / `.rin-*` /
  `.home-v2-mobile-signal` blocks are pinned EXACT.
- The ratchet (`tests/lib/type-material-tokens.test.ts`) only goes down; lower a
  sheet's pins when its stage lands. Raising one is an ADR line.
- Canvas text obeys via `lib/services-ring/ringType.ts`; the Bold face leaves the
  preload only after all three bakes are at 400.
- Light re-derives alphas, never inherits them (ADR-058).

Verify: `npx vitest run tests/lib/type-material-tokens.test.ts` and
`node scripts/design-eval/mechanical.mjs --url / --scope ".fl-case" --exclude ".fl-pda"`
in both themes.
